<title>USA: Cuno Inc Q2 April 30 net rises slightly.</title>
<headline>Cuno Inc Q2 April 30 net rises slightly.</headline>
<dateline>MERIDEN, Conn 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>STATEMENTS OF CONSOLIDATED INCOME</p>
<p>			   Three Months Ended	Six Months Ended</p>
<p>		   (dollars in thousands, except share amounts)</p>
<p>				   April 30		April 30</p>
<p>			    1997	 1996	  1997	 1996</p>
<p> Net Sales	   $46,383     $45,090     $91,222    $86,094</p>
<p> Operating income    5,540	 4,988	 9,467	7,624</p>
<p>Net income	    3,290	 3,251	 5,355	5,102</p>
<p>Net income per share</p>
<p>   of common stock    0.24	  0.24	  0.39	 0.38</p>
<p>Weighted average</p>
<p>common shares</p>
<p> outstanding 13,850,347  13,565,922  13,829,978  13,565,922</p>
<p>Pro forma net income</p>
<p>per share of</p>
<p>   common stock (A)   0.24	  0.21	  0.39	 0.32</p>
<p>(A) Reflects a pro forma adjustment in interest expense and related taxes to account for the allocation of $30 million in parent company debt to CUNO, assuming the September 10, 1996 distribution had taken place on November 1, 1995.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
